{"answer": "The initiative targets several specific traffic problems:  \n\n- **Traffic congestion** \u2013 to be reduced overall.  \n- **Excessive wear on Harper Road** \u2013 caused by increased usage, to be alleviated by expanding and modernizing the road.  \n- **Need for traffic dispersion from Greenfield Bridge** \u2013 a new bridge (starting Nov\u202f15\u202f2023) will divert traffic and ease pressure on the existing bridge.  \n- **Poor traffic flow and long waiting times** \u2013 addressed by repaving, smart traffic\u2011management systems, and adaptive signal controls at key intersections.  \n- **Construction\u2011related disruption** \u2013 mitigated through an Intelligent Transportation System (real\u2011time monitoring, adaptive traffic control, dynamic message signs) that informs drivers during peak hours or work zones.", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 2, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "zxdlsong-q1::chain_hop::node23::attempt1", "ts_monotonic": 224551.745644868, "ts_unix": 1777954487.9331493, "worker_id": "node23"}
{"answer": "Vancouver\u2019s road and bridge upgrade initiative targets several specific traffic problems:  \n\n- General traffic congestion (including peak\u2011hour congestion)  \n- Significant wear and overuse of Harper Road due to increased traffic  \n- Congestion on Greenfield Bridge, necessitating a new bridge to disperse traffic  \n- Disruptions caused by ongoing construction work  \n- Poor traffic flow and long waiting times at key intersections  \n\nThe plan addresses these by expanding/modernizing Harper Road, building a new bridge, repaving roads, and deploying smart traffic\u2011management systems (real\u2011time monitoring, adaptive signal control, dynamic message signs).", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 2, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "zxdlsong-q1::chain_hop::node23::attempt2", "ts_monotonic": 224567.489330414, "ts_unix": 1777954503.6768348, "worker_id": "node23"}
